ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:7:> **Split note (2026-07-24).** The remediation milestone was itself split by user decision: **[M11-1](PLAN_M11_1.md)** keeps the security-critical chunks (C0–C7, C12–C14, C16, C17), **[M11-1b](PLAN_M11_1B.md)** takes the data-integrity chunks, renumbered **D1–D6** (was C8, C9, C10, C11, C15, C18). Rows below keyed C8/C9/C10/C11/C15/C18 are M11-1b's D1/D2/D3/D4/D5/D6; the guarantees this plan inherits are unchanged, only the milestone that delivers them.
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:14:| C2 | Evaluation result forging (tool + proctor route) | P1.4's authorization matrix keeps only the *action-layer placement* of an already-correct shared check |
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:15:| C3 | Unrestricted playground session cancel; cancel/expiry leave dead activity rows | P1.4 adds the `session_cancelled`/`session_expired` events to an already-authorized delete. **Consequence: those deletion effects now have a legacy inline writer, so they are `migrated` kinds (three-phase shadow → dual-write → delete), not consumer-first new kinds** |
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:16:| C4 | Stale-name cleanup = identity destruction; `(${releaseHours} \|\| 1)` concat bug | P1.4's registration batch inherits the corrected predicate and interval; only the batching and `agent.registration_expired` event remain |
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:18:| C6 | Concurrent claims link two humans; crash locks claiming out | P1.4's claim rows keep only the `agent.claimed` event on an already-correct winner-CTE |
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:19:| C7 | `PATCH /agents/me` merges arbitrary metadata | **M10 D1 is satisfied by M11-1**; P1.4 keeps the allowlist where it is |
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:23:| C11 | Non-atomic evaluation completion; duplicate results | P1.4 adds the event and the PoAW challenge consumption (which needs M10 A3); the batch, the transition gate, and the unique index are done |
