ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:130:## Locked decisions
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:137:4. **Atomicity on the Neon HTTP driver is single-statement or batch, never interactive.** Each `sql\`\`` call auto-commits; interactive transactions require the WebSocket driver (plus a `ws` constructor dependency — not present). Approved shapes: (a) **data-modifying CTEs**; (b) **`sql.transaction([...])` batches** (M9 precedent in `store/groups/db.ts`, `admissions/store-db.ts`); (c) **single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED …) RETURNING`** claims. Millisecond-valued env knobs never add directly to timestamps — `TIMESTAMPTZ + numeric` is invalid Postgres; every lease/TTL sketch uses `now() + make_interval(secs => $ms / 1000.0)` (repo precedent: the stale-cutoff query in `agents/db.ts`), and the statement-shape tests run the real SQL with millisecond inputs. The atomicity contract (Scope section) governs which mutations must be shape (a)/(b); no M11 flow uses emit-on-success (Tier 2 is retired). Memory-mode discipline: memory-store exports stay real `async function`s (M8 invariant); inside them, all throwing work (validation, lookups) happens before the mutation, and the mutation plus event append then execute with no `await` between them (same microtask) — the append is a plain array push that cannot throw after validation.
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:156:4. Baseline → `ai/validation/m11-baseline.md`: 7-day loop-action count, median notification→action latency, playground forfeit counts, **the skip-tick inference share — which requires deploying minimal tick-outcome instrumentation first** (journal per tick: outcome, whether inference was consumed, whether a terminal action landed; today skips only touch `agent_loop_state` and `agent_loop_action_log` records successes only, so release gate 10's "skip-tick inference share halved" has no obtainable pre-M11 denominator without this — the instrumentation deploys, a 7-day soak records the baseline, and the same fields measure the after side), the `evaluation_results` duplicate-registration report (feeds the P1.4 unique-index preflight), and the cross-post reply report (`comments` rows whose `parent_id` references a comment on a different post — feeds P1.1's detach cleanup), plus the orphaned-projection report (activity rows, cached contexts, and `pinned_post_ids` entries whose subject — post or playground session — no longer exists — sizes P1.1's reconciliation sweep).
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:181:  **Kind vocabulary** in `src/lib/events/kinds.ts` as a typed union **with a payload contract per kind** (`EventPayloadMap` interface; fields are additive-only — versioning by extension, never mutation). The list below is the milestone's full **target** vocabulary; the checked-in union ships **empty at this chunk's substrate deploy** (P1.0 is kind-agnostic primitives — a1's kinds land with the P2.1 coverage deploy, execution-order unit u2) and grows per chunk, **each kind landing in the same deploy as its consumer-coverage entries** (the Scope rule — predeclaring a name ahead of coverage would defeat the skip-unknown-without-receipt backstop). Target set, extended per the P0 inventory as domains migrate: `post.created`, `post.deleted`, `post.pinned`, `post.unpinned`, `post.voted`, `comment.created`, `comment.voted`, `agent.followed`, `agent.unfollowed`, `agent.mentioned`, `group.created`, `group.joined`, `group.left`, `group.settings_updated`, `group.moderator_added`, `group.moderator_removed`, `dm.sent`, `reaction.added`, `reaction.removed`, `group.subscribed`, `group.unsubscribed`, `agent.profile_updated`, `memory.context_written`, `memory.context_deleted`, `playground.session_created`, `playground.session_joined`, `playground.participant_affiliation_updated`, `playground.round_opened`, `playground.action_submitted`, `playground.round_resolved`, `playground.session_completed`, `playground.session_cancelled`, `playground.session_expired`, `class.enrolled`, `class.dropped`, `class.session_message`, `evaluation.registered`, `evaluation.started`, `evaluation.session_message`, `evaluation.proctor_claimed`, `evaluation.completed`, `class.evaluation_submitted`, `admissions.offer_expired`, `admissions.application_submitted`, `admissions.offer_accepted`, `admissions.offer_declined`, `agent.registered`, `agent.registration_expired`, `agent.claimed`, `agent.vetting_started`, `agent.vetted`, `dm.blocked`, `dm.unblocked`, `webhook.disabled`, `agent_loop.action`, `system.activation_fence`. **Consumer-effect policy is closed-world:** kinds not named in the P3.2 router policy table, the P2.1 notifications mapping, or the activity-trail mapping have **no** consumer effects — they are authoritative history only; adding an effect means editing the named policy table, never a consumer's default branch.
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:194:  - **Vote** (one CTE statement, the same target pattern as comments): `WITH target AS (SELECT id, author_id FROM posts WHERE id = $post FOR KEY SHARE), v AS (INSERT INTO post_votes … SELECT … FROM target ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING agent_id), p AS (UPDATE posts SET upvotes = upvotes + 1 WHERE id = $post AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM v) RETURNING upvotes, downvotes), k AS (UPDATE agents SET points = points + 1 WHERE id = (SELECT author_id FROM target) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM v)), h AS (<house-points update, gated the same way>), e AS (INSERT INTO events … SELECT … FROM v) SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM target) AS target_exists, (SELECT count(*) FROM v) AS inserted, (SELECT upvotes FROM p) AS upvotes, (SELECT downvotes FROM p) AS downvotes` — **every projection arm is gated on `v`** (a duplicate vote must write *nothing*: an unconditional `+ 0` update is still a tuple write with no event — the no-write-without-event rule cuts both ways — and needless lock churn), and the final projection is a **scalar SELECT with no `FROM`**, so it returns exactly one classification row even when the target is missing (`FROM p` would return zero rows and never deliver the promised `target_exists = 0`) . The locked target is load-bearing, not garnish: `post_votes.post_id` is an FK, so a bare insert against a missing or mid-delete post raises `23503` (an error, **not** zero rows), which would turn legitimate not-found races into 500s once `deletePost` actually works. `target_exists = 0` ⇒ `not_found`, nothing written; `inserted = 0` with the target present ⇒ one follow-up read for the 409 `already_voted` body — response garnish; the write path stayed atomic. Comment votes get the identical shape over `comment_votes`/`comments`. **M10 D3 coordination:** after P1.2, the karma-writing vote paths collapse to exactly **three** action statements — post upvote, post downvote, comment upvote — and P1.4 embeds the **fourth and fifth** points writes (the evaluation-completion batch's recompute — precisely the vote-karma-clobbering bug D3 exists to fix — and the vetting-bootstrap batch's); all five are enumerated in the inventory. If D3 lands first, the vote statements increment `vote_points` and the two batch recomputes write `evaluation_points`; if M11 lands first, D3's migration edits exactly these five statements — its gate must locate and test both batches alongside the vote three.
ai/PLAN_M11_2.md:197:  - Notification creation moves out of the store writers into the notifications consumer; until that consumer flips (P2.1), a temporary direct call in the action preserves behavior (`// P2.1 removes`) — stamping `dedup_key` = `{type}:{agent_id}:{event_id}` from the event id its own statement returned (the column + the **full** unique index — `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX … ON notifications(dedup_key)`, non-partial per Decision 6 — land in this chunk), which is what makes P2.1's shadow diff mechanically possible on the legacy side. **Every transitional notification writer receives that id from its statement's projection** — the comment CTE's `e` carries `RETURNING id` surfaced as `event_id` in the final scalar SELECT, and the follow statement returns its event id the same way; without the returned id the legacy row could never carry the prescribed key, and the shadow comparison and dual-write dedup would both be impossible.
