   326	/**
   327	 * M11-1b D6, memory mode — every check and every mutation in ONE synchronous section.
   328	 *
   329	 * The pre-D6 shape `await`ed the cap count before mutating, and "single-threaded" is not atomic
   330	 * across an `await`: two concurrent promises both counted, both found room, and both inserted. The
   331	 * db side serializes on the cycle row; here the equivalent is simply never yielding between the
   332	 * decision and the write. Stale pending offers are expired first for the same reason as db mode —
   333	 * the cap counts every pending row, so lapsed ones would eat the cycle's capacity.
