    96	    // phase here is bounded by a row count, and a row count is not a time bound: a consumer with a
    97	    // permanent backlog fills its batch on every invocation and consumes the invocation's whole
    98	    // budget, so duties queued behind it would never run at all. That would starve the below-floor
