Verdict: The u3f-core slice is not ready. I found three BLOCKER defects and seven MAJOR defects. The manifests and the Postgres accept event gate are correct. I reviewed commit `682e40a`. I did not run tests or modify files.

1. **BLOCKER — The database expiry duty breaks the global lock order.**  
   [store-db.ts:103](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-db.ts:103)

   The statement locks offers before agents. An agent deletion can lock the application first and then wait for the offer. The expiry duty can hold the offer and wait for that application. PostgreSQL can then report `40P01`.

   Minimal fix: Add an ordered `sweep_agents` CTE. Lock each agent `FOR KEY SHARE` before `expired` updates offers.

2. **BLOCKER — The memory expiry driver emits no event and can release an active application.**  
   [store-memory.ts:89](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-memory.ts:89)  
   [store-memory.ts:311](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-memory.ts:311)

   The public driver uses the first function. That function does not append `admissions.offer_expired`. It also returns an application to `in_pool` without a live-offer check.

   A legacy application with one expired offer and one live offer becomes `in_pool`. The live offer still stands.

   Minimal fix: Use one shared expiry function. Preflight all per-offer events, apply the live-offer predicate, then append the full event batch.

3. **BLOCKER — A teaching assistant uses the agent branch and emits an event.**  
   [messages/route.ts:66](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/app/api/v1/classes/[id]/sessions/[sessionId]/messages/route.ts:66)  
   [actions/classes.ts:63](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/actions/classes.ts:63)

   The route only detects a professor. A teaching assistant reaches `sendSessionMessage`, receives the `ta` role, and emits `class.session_message`.

   This result conflicts with the required history-silent operator branch.

   Minimal fix: Detect the teaching assistant before the student branch. Send professor and assistant messages through `class-ops`.

4. **MAJOR — The class statements do not enforce the domain gates.**  
   [actions/classes.ts:28](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/actions/classes.ts:28)  
   [db.ts:337](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/store/classes/db.ts:337)  
   [db.ts:502](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/store/classes/db.ts:502)  
   [db.ts:642](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/store/classes/db.ts:642)

   The actions check capacity, session status, evaluation status, and enrollment through unlocked reads. The statements then write without those predicates.

   Two agents can both see one free seat. Both inserts and both events can commit. A completed session can also receive a late message.

   Minimal fix: Return outcome flags from locked statements. Gate each event on the statement row that passed every applicable rule.

5. **MAJOR — The database accept result comes from a later read.**  
   [store-db.ts:597](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-db.ts:597)  
   [store-db.ts:609](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-db.ts:609)

   An acceptance can commit its timestamp, audit row, and event. A decline can commit before `classifyAcceptOutcomeDb` reads the offer.

   The accept call then returns `invalid`, although its acceptance effects committed.

   Minimal fix: Return the acceptance outcome from a transaction element while the transaction still holds its locks.

6. **MAJOR — Memory acceptance yields before finalization.**  
   [store-memory.ts:440](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-memory.ts:440)

   The function waits for event dispatch before it calls `tryFinalizeOfferMem`. A concurrent decline can use this gap.

   A no-human offer can record acceptance and its event, then finish as `declined`. The database batch finishes admission before a decline can act.

   Minimal fix: Complete the synchronous finalization section before the first `await`. Wait for dispatch only after all related state changes.

7. **MAJOR — Concurrent memory pool ensures can create duplicate applications.**  
   [store-memory.ts:169](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/store-memory.ts:169)

   Two calls can both capture a missing application before the awaited lookup resumes. Both calls then create an application and an event.

   The `appKey` map keeps one ID, but the `apps` map and event log keep both. PostgreSQL permits only one row.

   Minimal fix: Recheck the agent map and `appKey` in one synchronous section after the final `await`.

8. **MAJOR — Several mutation paths still bypass the action boundary.**  
   [admissions/index.ts:184](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/admissions/index.ts:184)  
   [accept/route.ts:31](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/app/api/v1/admissions/accept/route.ts:31)  
   [classes.ts:263](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/agent-tools/definitions/classes.ts:263)  
   [classes.ts:300](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/agent-tools/definitions/classes.ts:300)  
   [classes/[id]/route.ts:8](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/app/api/v1/classes/[id]/route.ts:8)

   The status service creates the application event directly. The planned `ensurePoolApplication` action has no caller.

   The accept route, decline route, and two class tools also decide missing-resource refusals before their actions. The class-detail file still imports `updateClass`.

   Minimal fix: Move child resolution and the lazy ensure into actions. Move the remaining operator update behind `class-ops`.

9. **MAJOR — The adapters change legacy response shapes.**  
   [actions/admissions.ts:15](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/actions/admissions.ts:15)  
   [application/route.ts:33](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/app/api/v1/admissions/application/route.ts:33)  
   [actions/classes.ts:20](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/lib/actions/classes.ts:20)

   For example, no open cycle now returns HTTP 409. The legacy route returned HTTP 503. Several hints and school-denial fields also disappear.

   Minimal fix: Add stable reason values to the action results. Make each adapter map those reasons to its exact legacy status, title, hint, and fields.

10. **MAJOR — The scoped tests do not prove the required coupling.**  
    [m11-2-u3f-core-characterization.test.ts:5](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/__tests__/lib/m11-2-u3f-core-characterization.test.ts:5)  
    [ux6-contracts.test.ts:350](/Users/mohsin/Github/safemolt/src/__tests__/api/v1/ux6-contracts.test.ts:350)

    The core test checks import text only. The UX6 case checks that the action passes an event to a mocked store.

    No scoped test covers rollback, no-op events, expiry parity, lock order, the assistant split, or memory acceptance races.

    Minimal fix: Add statement-shape tests, event-failure tests, no-op tests, and memory race tests for each Tier-1 producer.
